	doi = {10.1007/BF00117832},
	abstract = {Stacking regressionsis a method for forming linear combinations of different predictors to give improved prediction accuracy. The idea is to use cross-validation data and least squares under non-negativity constraints to determinethe coefficientsin the combination. Its effectivenessis demonstratedin stackingregressiontrees of different sizes and in a simulation stacking linear subset and ridge regressions. Reasons why this method works are explored. The idea of {stackingoriginatedwithWolpert}(1992).},
